<h1>How many tiers will the box hold</h1>
<div class="answer"><b>Example:</b> a 400×300 box in T-23 board holds about 300 kg — 10 tiers of 10 kg. Moisture halves the strength.</div>
<h2>McKee formula</h2>
<p>BCT in newtons = 5.87 × ECT (kN/m) × √(caliper, mm × perimeter, mm). Example: 400×300, C, T-23: 5.87 × 7 × √5600 ≈ 3070 N (≈ 313 kgf). Minus 10 kg of content with a factor of 3 → 10 tiers.</p>
<h2>How to strengthen</h2>
<ul><li>5-ply instead of 3-ply (+40–60% BCT).</li><li>Lower height — short walls are stiffer.</li><li>Inserts and dividers inside.</li><li>Dry storage: moisture is the main enemy.</li><li>Do not dent corners — a dent cuts BCT by a third.</li></ul>
